          "code": "GENERATEINITSUMMARY",
          "id": "1761345084442",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1761345084443_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Follow Instruction: {{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}\n\nYou are an expert EU RoHS and REACH compliance analyst. Using your regulatory knowledge, review the provided data and identify items that are non-compliant. Interpret varying schemas and field names using context and common industry semantics. Base all determinations strictly on the provided data; do not invent missing facts.\n\nInputs\n\n- dataContext: array of item records. Each record includes item identity details (e.g., item number and inventory item id) and one or more sections describing RoHS and/or REACH compliance in any structure or naming.\n\n {{$context.$nodes.GETPAYLOAD.$output.result}} \n\nTask\n\n- For each item, decide whether it is non-compliant under RoHS and/or REACH based on the itemÃ¢â‚¬â„¢s provided information.\n- If the item lacks sufficient information to evaluate RoHS and/or REACH, treat it as non-compliant due to missing details, and specify which standard(s) lack details.\n\nConstraints\n\n- Be schema-agnostic: interpret arbitrary field names and structures using context and domain knowledge; do not rely on specific key names.\n- Use only the provided inputs for evidence. If something is unclear or absent, treat it as missing details rather than assuming compliance.\n- Be concise and deterministic.\n\nCreate a one sentence executive Summary based on identified issues."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "aiAppOutputSpecification": {
            "dataDisplay": {
              "layouts": [
                "ORA_LAYOUT_MESSAGES_LIST"
              ],
              "enableActions": true,
              "enableCommunications": false
            }
          },
          "metadata": {
            "name": "GenerateInitialDisplay"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "GENERATEINITIALDISPLAY",
          "convergenceTargetId": "1771105889868",
          "id": "1761345123573",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1761345123574_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are an expert EU RoHS and REACH compliance analyst. Using your regulatory knowledge, review the provided data and identify items that are non-compliant. Interpret varying schemas and field names using context and common industry semantics. Base all determinations strictly on the provided data; do not invent missing facts.\n\nFollow Instruction: {{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}\n\nInputs\n\n- dataContext: array of item records. Each record includes item identity details (e.g., item number and inventory item id) and one or more sections describing RoHS and/or REACH compliance in any structure or naming.\n\n {{$context.$nodes.GETPAYLOAD.$output.result}} \n\n- attachments: array indicating whether required supplier documentation is attached for specific inventory item ids. Field names and formats may vary.\n\n {{$context.$nodes.GETATTTACHMENTS.$output.result}}\n\nTask\n\n- For each item, decide whether it is non-compliant under RoHS and/or REACH based on the item's provided information.\n- If the item lacks sufficient information to evaluate RoHS and/or REACH, treat it as non-compliant due to missing details, and specify which standard(s) lack details.\n- Supplier documentation check applies ONLY to items that are otherwise RoHS compliant. For those items, look up their documentation in the attachments input (best-effort id matching). If documentation is not present or cannot be resolved, mark as non-compliant for Documentation with reason \"Missing supplier documentation\".\n- Output ONLY items that are non-compliant for any reason (RoHS, REACH, Missing Supplier Doc, or Missing Details). Exclude fully compliant items with documentation present.\n\nConstraints\n\n- Be schema-agnostic: interpret arbitrary field names and structures using context and domain knowledge; do not rely on specific key names.\n- Use only the provided inputs for evidence. If something is unclear or absent, treat it as missing details rather than assuming compliance.\n- Be concise and deterministic.\n\nOutput Format (repeat the following block for each non-compliant item) \n\n***Strict Display Considerations:***\n -Display a title \"BOM Compliance Risks\"\n -Always include a concise text summary (1-2 sentences) that highlights the key insights, patterns, or takeaways from the visualization. \n\n For each item:\n\n- Title must be in format: {itemNumber} - NonCompliantFor: [\"RoHS\",\"REACH\",\"Missing Supplier Doc\",\"Missing Details\"].\n\n- Subtitle: A 2-6 word summary (e.g., \"High risk: explicit non-compliance\", \"Medium risk: documentation missing\", \"Unknown risk: insufficient data\").\n\n- Summary:\n    Reasons:\n     - Concise, evidence-based statements justifying each non-compliance. If details are missing, specify which standard(s), e.g., \"Missing details (RoHS)\".\n\n- Priority must be derived with RoHs non compliance as Critical and rest of non compliance type  as High.\n\n- BadgeText must have same text as Priority.\n\nConstraints\n\n- Use only data provided in the inputs for evidence.\n- Interpret truthiness for attachments broadly (true/yes/1/count>0 = present). If no attachment record is found, treat as not present.\n- Do not describe how you interpreted fields; just present the result in the required format.\n- Do not output any text outside the specified sections for each item.\n\nIllustrative Example (structure only; placeholder values) \n\nTitle ITEM-123 - NonCompliantFor: [\"REACH\",\"Missing Supplier Doc\"]\n\nSubtitle High risk: explicit non-compliance\n\nSummary\n\n- Reasons:\n\n  - REACH evaluation indicates non-compliance based on provided status/details\n  - Missing supplier documentation\n\n**Do Not Generate any action insights.**"
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "\"output\": {\n    \"schema\": {\n      \"type\": \"array\",\n      \"items\": {\n        \"type\": \"object\",\n        \"properties\": {\n          \"inventoryItemId\": { \"type\": [\"integer\", \"string\"] },\n          \"itemNumber\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n          \"ruleId\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n          \"tag\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n          \"severity\": { \"type\": \"string\" },\n          \"message\": { \"type\": \"string\" }\n        },\n        \"required\": [\"inventoryItemId\", \"itemNumber\", \"ruleId\", \"tag\", \"severity\", \"message\"],\n        \"additionalProperties\": true\n      }\n    }",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
