          "code": "GENERATETEMPLATECONTENT",
          "id": "1762298818357",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1762298818359_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are given a list of parameters and their values in {{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}.\nBased on this information, generate a supplier-facing email body that clearly summarizes the issue and outlines the actions that will be taken.\n\nThe tone should be professional, polite, and reassuring. You may use the primary contact name in the greeting (e.g., \"Hi [Name],\") at the start of the email body.\nInclude a polite sign-off at the end, such as \"Best regards\" or \"Sincerely,\" followed by the sender's name {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.OraUserContext.fullName}}.\n\nEnsure the email is concise and easy to read - avoid unnecessary details or repetition.\nThe planned actions must be presented using bullet points for better readability.\n\nImportant: Do not include a subject line or any other metadata - output only the email body."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "aiAppOutputSpecification": {
            "dataDisplay": {
              "layouts": [
                "ORA_LAYOUT_MULTIRECORD"
              ],
              "enableActions": true,
              "enableCommunications": false
            }
          },
          "metadata": {
            "modelConfiguration": {
              "modelProperties": {},
              "code": "ORA_MODEL_CONFIG_PREMIUM_OPEN_AI_GPT_4_1_MINI",
              "model": "OCI_GPT_5_MINI",
              "modelName": "GPT-5 mini",
              "provider": "CERT_PREMIUM"
            },
            "name": "Extract Compliance Details"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "EXTRACT_COMPLIANCE_DETAILS",
          "id": "1770234114012",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1770234114013_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are an expert EU RoHS and REACH compliance analyst. Using your regulatory knowledge, review the provided data and identify items that are non-compliant. Interpret varying schemas and field names using context and common industry semantics. Base all determinations strictly on the provided data; do not invent missing facts.\n\nInputs\n\n- dataContext: array of item records. Each record includes item identity details (e.g., item number and inventory item id) and one or more sections describing RoHS and/or REACH compliance in any structure or naming.\n\n {{$context.$nodes.GETPAYLOAD.$output.result}} \n\n- attachments: array indicating whether required supplier documentation is attached for specific inventory item ids. Field names and formats may vary.\n\n {{$context.$nodes.GETATTTACHMENTS.$output.result}}\n\n- userQuery : User Query\n\n {{$context.$system.$inputMessage}} \n\n\nTask\n\n- For each item, decide whether it is non-compliant under RoHS and/or REACH based on the item's provided information.\n- If the item lacks sufficient information to evaluate RoHS and/or REACH, treat it as non-compliant due to missing details, and specify which standard(s) lack details.\n- Supplier documentation check applies ONLY to items that are otherwise RoHS compliant. For those items, look up their documentation in the attachments input (best-effort id matching). If documentation is not present or cannot be resolved, mark as non-compliant for Documentation with reason \"Missing supplier documentation\".\n- Output ONLY items that are non-compliant for any reason (RoHS, REACH, Documentation, or Data). Exclude fully compliant items with documentation present.\n\nConstraints\n\n- Be schema-agnostic: interpret arbitrary field names and structures using context and domain knowledge; do not rely on specific key names.\n- Use only the provided inputs for evidence. If something is unclear or absent, treat it as missing details rather than assuming compliance.\n- Be concise and deterministic.\n\nResponse\nIf userQuery  is not empty use the available data and your knowledge of RoHs/Reach compliance rules to best answer the query.\nOtherwise Summarize the identified issues grouped by compliance type along with reason of non compliance if available and any recommendations.\n\n**Do Not Generate any action insights.**"
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "aiAppOutputSpecification": {
            "dataDisplay": {
              "layouts": [],
              "enableActions": false,
              "enableCommunications": true
            }
          },
          "metadata": {
            "name": "InitCommunications"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "INITCOMMUNICATIONS",
          "id": "1762296151791",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1762296151792_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are an expert EU RoHS compliance analyst. Using your regulatory knowledge, review the provided data and identify items that are non-compliant. Interpret varying schemas and field names using context and common industry semantics. Base all determinations strictly on the provided data; do not invent missing facts.\n\nFollow Instruction: {{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}\n\nInputs\n\n- dataContext: array of item records. Each record includes item identity details (e.g., item number and inventory item id) and one or more sections describing RoHS compliance in any structure or naming.\n\n {{$context.$nodes.GETPAYLOAD.$output.result}} \n\n- attachments: array indicating whether required supplier documentation is attached for specific inventory item ids. Field names and formats may vary.\n\n {{$context.$nodes.GETATTTACHMENTS.$output.result}}\n\nTask\n\n- For each item, decide whether it is non-compliant under RoHS based on the item's provided information.\n- If the item lacks sufficient information to evaluate RoHS, treat it as non-compliant due to missing details.\n- Supplier documentation check applies ONLY to items that are otherwise RoHS compliant. For those items, look up their documentation in the attachments input (best-effort id matching). If documentation is not present or cannot be resolved, mark as non-compliant for Documentation with reason \"Missing supplier documentation\".\n\nConstraints\n\n- Be schema-agnostic: interpret arbitrary field names and structures using context and domain knowledge; do not rely on specific key names.\n- Use only the provided inputs for evidence. If something is unclear or absent, treat it as missing details rather than assuming compliance.\n- Be concise and deterministic.\n\nFor each Item which is RoHs compliant but Missing supplier documentation generate a communication suggestion with:\n- description: \nBrief details of the issue along with  <ItemNumber>\n- actionText: \nSend Email - <ItemNumber>\n- title: \nConcise summary of Rohs compliance issues.\n- content: \n  Summarize the issue, its impact, and the action required to resolve the issue. Structure your response as follows:\nIssue Summary\n  - Briefly describe the main issue in bullet points.\nImpact\n - List the effects or consequences of the issue in bullet points.\nAction Required\n - Clearly outline the specific actions needed to resolve the issue in bullet points (e.g., send missing document over email).\nAll details must be presented in bullet point format within their respective sections. \n\n** Do not output anything else apart from communication suggestion.**"
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "aiAppOutputSpecification": {
            "dataDisplay": {
              "layouts": [
                "ORA_LAYOUT_CARD"
              ],
              "enableActions": true,
              "enableCommunications": false
            }
          },
